{title: As the Deer (FJ_181_en)}
{song_number: 181}
{language: en}
{key: D}
{tempo: 68}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]As the deer pants [A]for [Bm]the water, so my [Em]soul longs [A7]after [D]You.
[D]You alone [A]are my [Bm]heart's desire and I [G]long to [A7]worship [D]You.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bm]You alone are my [G]strength, my shield; [D]to
[G]You alone may my [Em]spirit [F#]yield.
[D]You alone [A]are my [Bm]heart's desire and I [G]long to [A7]worship [D]You.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]I want You more [A]than [Bm]gold or silver, only [Em]You can [A7]satisfy. [D]
[D]You alone [A]are the [Bm]real joy-giver and the [G]apple [A7]of my [D]eye.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bm]You alone are my [G]strength, my shield; [D]to
[G]You alone may my [Em]spirit [F#]yield.
[D]You alone [A]are my [Bm]heart's desire and I [G]long to [A7]worship [D]You.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]You're my friend [A]and [Bm]You're my brother, even [Em]though You [A7]are a [D]king.
[D]I love You [A]more than [Bm]any other, so much [G]more than [A7]anything. [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bm]You alone are my [G]strength, my shield; [D]to
[G]You alone may my [Em]spirit [F#]yield.
[D]You alone [A]are my [Bm]heart's desire and I [G]long to [A7]worship [D]You.
{end_of_chorus}
